  x-verified = {Verified 2026-09-20 and read in full text from the author's scan. Theorem 1 is the anomaly bound; the list-scheduling makespan ratio 2 - 1/n appears as a remark on page 421 and not as a numbered theorem, and Theorem 2 is the LPT bound 4/3 - 1/(3n). The additive form, makespan at most the optimum plus (1 - 1/n) times the processing time of the last task to finish, occurs inside the proof of Theorem 2 on page 422 and only where the precedence order is empty. The manuscript therefore cites the ratio as the stated result and the additive form as a step in that proof. Graham writes n for the number of processors}
